From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kossLAN <kosslan@kosslan.dev>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:30:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] virtio-gpu-gl: replace no surface in the vCPU thread on
 reset

A guest resetting virtio-gpu-gl (Windows does while it boots) ran
virtio_gpu_virgl_reset_scanout() in the vCPU thread, and its
qemu_console_set_surface() made the new surface's GL texture there,
where no GL context is current: the texture was 0, and a D-Bus display
listener attached at the time aborted QEMU in dbus_scanout_texture()
(assert(tex_id)).

virtio_gpu_reset() has already replaced the surfaces in the main thread
(virtio_gpu_reset_bh). Disabling the GL scanout stays here; the D-Bus
display does no GL work for it.

Signed-off-by: kossLAN <kosslan@kosslan.dev>
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index 6e298f997..2ec7cb0b9 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -1402,8 +1402,8 @@ void virtio_gpu_virgl_reset_scanout(VirtIOGPU *g)
 {
     int i;
 
+    /* Called in a vCPU thread, where no GL context is current. */
     for (i = 0; i < g->parent_obj.conf.max_outputs; i++) {
-        qemu_console_set_surface(g->parent_obj.scanout[i].con, NULL);
         qemu_console_gl_scanout_disable(g->parent_obj.scanout[i].con);
     }
 }
